# fixedbugs, defect 2034, 2026-10-12; written as defect 569's follow-up on
# lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (after panel 205's R2), at 2067ec87.
#
# The name keeps 569 because the case was written under that number, on a
# branch never merged, and the 569 issue's follow-up record names it so;
# defect 2034 is that repair found unmerged and landed, and its new cases
# beside this one carry 2034.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf` takes a `char *`
# for `%d` built under the ratified region, which ignored `-Wformat` with
# the rest of `-Wall`, and printed a pointer's low bits (48670265 on
# 2026-10-10, 34551295 on 2026-10-12) at exit 0: undefined behaviour in
# code the program runs, told by nothing.
#
# FIX: `-Wformat` stays an error in the region (`emit/header_region.hero`'s
# `KEPT`), beside a missing return and an uninitialised read, on the
# coordinator's ruling of the lane's question.

extern "fixedbugs-569-a-header-of-the-program-s-own-with-a-mismatched-format-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shout() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shout())
